COMMAND NAME: mpprebuildseg.sh

Rebuilds segment instances from the Greenplum system catalog tables of a 
Greenplum Database master instance.


*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mpprebuildseg.sh -d <master_data_directory> [-n <locale>] [-a] [-q] 
[-l <logfile_directory>] [-D] [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mpprebuildseg.sh script builds segment instances using configuration 
information contained in the Greenplum system catalog tables of a Greenplum 
Database master instance. The use of this script assumes that you have:

1. Built a master instance from a backup file using mpprebuildcluster.sh -m.

2. Have edited the Greenplum system catalog tables on the Greenplum master 
   instance to reflect your desired system configuration. See the 
   Greenplum Database Administrator Guide for more information.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-d <master_data_directory>

Required. The data directory of the Greenplum master instance.


-n <locale>

Sets the default locale (character set encoding) for the Greenplum Database 
system. Defaults to en_US.utf8 (UNICODE). You must make sure that the 
locale you specify exists on your operating system (locale -a will show 
which locales are available). See 'Character Set Support' in the 
PostgreSQL documentation for more information on the supported character 
set encodings.


-a (do not prompt)

Do not prompt the user for confirmation.


-q (no screen output)

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, but is 
still written to the log file.


-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.


-D (debug)

Sets logging level to debug.


-? (help)

Displays the online help.


-v (show script version)

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Rebuild the segment instances using the data found in the given Greenplum 
master:

mpprebuildseg.sh -d /dbfast1/master/gp-1


